---
// News: one post per event of note, newest first, with the opening post pinned at the top (tracker
// pattern, rules 4.10 to 4.13; ruled by John 2026-10-18). Copied on 2026-11-21 from Outrunning
// Ageing's site/src/pages/news/index.astro, the model the sibling sites copied. Its wording is
// PROPOSED (docs/proposals/2026-11-21-news-section.md). The foot points at "Everything, by date",
// which lists every dated act whether or not a post explains it, as the sibling's foot points at
// its story so far.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../../styles/news.css';
import { longDate } from '../../lib/data';
import { datedPosts, opener, postPath, KIND_LABEL, wordCount } from '../../lib/news';

const posts = await datedPosts();
const start = await opener();
---

<Base title="News · Beyond the Window" description="What changed in the record, and why: one post for each change a reader would want explained, with what happened, where the record is, and what it changes on this site.">
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">News</p>
    <h1>What changed in the record, and why</h1>
    <p class="lede">A post is written when something a reader would want explained changes here. That may be the count on the home page: how many of the things a developer can do in how it treats the AI models it builds are done, or publicly committed to, by at least one developer today. It may be where one of those things stands, a new entry in the record, or a change to the way the record is kept. A post may also tell a story from the field that a reader would care about, whether or not it changes anything on this site. Each post says what happened and links its sources, and a post about a change names the entries it changed.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    {start && (
      <div class="opener">
        <span class="k">Start here</span>
        <h3><a href={postPath(start)}>{start.data.title}</a></h3>
        <p>{start.data.summary}</p>
        <p class="meta">{longDate(start.data.date)} · about {Math.round(wordCount(start.body) / 100) * 100} words · <a href={postPath(start)}>read it</a></p>
      </div>
    )}
    {posts.length === 0 ? (
      <p class="empty-note">No post yet. The first is written the day something of note changes.</p>
    ) : (
      <ul class="news-list">
        {posts.map((p) => (
          <li class="news-item">
            <time datetime={p.data.date}>{p.data.date}</time><span class="kind">{KIND_LABEL[p.data.kind]}</span>
            <h3><a href={postPath(p)}>{p.data.title}</a></h3>
            <p>{p.data.summary}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    )}
    <p class="news-foot">Every dated act in the record, including the ones no post explains, is in <a href="/acts/">everything, by date</a>, newest first.</p>
    <p class="news-follow">Follow the news: <a href="/news/feed.xml">the feed</a> · <a href="https://x.com/SentHorizons" rel="noopener">@SentHorizons on X</a> · <a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/SentientHorizons/" rel="noopener">r/SentientHorizons on Reddit</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
